research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13394-theorem.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13395-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13396-**Where the sign hypothesis enters.**
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13397-[[thm-nonnegative-series-bounded-partial-sums]] is the pivot of the page: for
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13398-nonnegative terms the partial sums are nondecreasing, so convergence is exactly
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13399-boundedness above of the partial sums, and the sum is their supremum. Every test
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13400-that follows is an application of it. [[thm-direct-comparison-test]] compares
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log:13401:against an arbitrary series, [[thm-limit-comparison-test]] does the same through
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13402-the quotient $a_k/b_k$, phrasing the infinite case as divergence to $+\infty$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13403-([[def-divergence-to-infinity]]) rather than as an extended limit equation, and
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13404-[[thm-cauchy-condensation]] reindexes instead of comparing, squeezing blocks of
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13405-$2^{n}$ terms between $2^{n}$ copies of the first and $2^{n}$ copies of the last.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13406-Condensation settles the whole $p$-series family at a stroke:
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13407-[[thm-p-series-rational]] proves that $\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/k^{p}$ converges exactly
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13408-when $p > 1$, for every rational $p > 0$, which is every exponent this page can
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-rem-strength-order-of-the-nonnegative-tests.log-13409-name ([[def-rational-power]]).
