research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-thm-limit-comparison-test.prompt.md-217-  "rationale": "The University of North Dakota theorem gives all three regimes: positive finite limit gives common behaviour, zero gives convergence only from the comparison series to the smaller one, and infinity gives divergence only from the comparison series to the larger one. The item uses real convergence versus divergence to +infinity explicitly, adds contrapositives, and shifts from index 1 to 0. Its proof follows the standard eventual two-sided inequalities.",
