research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.prompt.md-146-[L1] The canonical naturals $\iota(k+1)$ are positive, so $a_k, b_k > 0$; and reciprocation on the positives is order reversing ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.prompt.md-147-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.prompt.md-148-[L2] For every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a natural $n \ge 1$ with $1/n < \varepsilon$ ([[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]], [[def-real-limit]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.prompt.md-149-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.prompt.md-150-[L3] $\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/k^{p}$ converges if and only if $p > 1$; at $p = 2$ it converges ([[thm-p-series-rational]], [[def-rational-power]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.prompt.md-151-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional.prompt.md-152-[L4] The harmonic series $\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/k$ diverges, and it is the series of $j \mapsto 1/\iota(j+1)$ ([[ex-harmonic-series-diverges]], [[def-series]]).
