research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-642312-+          "quote": "the finite sum of [[def-finite-sum]]. In particular $s_0 = 0$, the empty sum, and\n$s_{n+1} = s_n + a_n$ for every $n$, those being exactly the two recursion clauses\nthat define the finite sum. Note that $s_n$ is the sum of the $n$ terms\n$a_0, \\dots, a_{n-1}$, so the index $n$ counts terms rather than naming the last\none.",
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-642313-+          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-642314-+            "1.3"
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-642315-+          ]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-642316-+        },
