research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-707902-+          ]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-707903-+        },
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-707904-+        {
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-707905-+          "fact": "L5",
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:707906:+          "source": "thm-limit-comparison-test",
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-707907-+          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-707908-+          "quote": "1. if $(q_k)$ converges with $\\lim_k q_k = L$ for a real $L > 0$\n   ([[def-real-limit]]), then $\\sum a_k$ converges **if and only if** $\\sum b_k$\n   converges;\n2. if $(q_k)$ converges with $\\lim_k q_k = 0$, then convergence of $\\sum b_k$\n   implies convergence of $\\sum a_k$; equivalently, divergence of $\\sum a_k$\n   implies divergence of $\\sum b_k$;\n3. if $(q_k)$ diverges to $+\\infty$ ([[def-divergence-to-infinity]]), then\n   convergence of $\\sum a_k$ implies convergence of $\\sum b_k$; equivalently,\n   divergence of $\\sum b_k$ implies divergence of $\\sum a_k$.",
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-707909-+          "uses": [
